$DIR/test.p:4:29: invalid break label L
    This error occurs when a break or continue label is not on a for, switch, or
    select statement.
    (see "Labeled statements" in the Plutonium spec, section 12.3)
    (run "pluto explain E0121" for a longer explanation)

$DIR/test.p:6:7: goto M jumps over variable declaration at line 7
    This error occurs when a label jumps over a variable declaration.
    (see "Goto statements" in the Plutonium spec, section 12.17)
    (run "pluto explain E0123" for a longer explanation)

$DIR/test.p:7:24: goto M jumps over variable declaration at line 7
    (explained above; run "pluto explain E0123" for more)

$DIR/test.p:3:1: label L declared and not used
    A label is declared but no break, continue or goto uses it. Remove it.
    (see "Labeled statements" in the Plutonium spec, section 12.3)
    (run "pluto explain E0122" for a longer explanation)
